statement:
Let $P$ be a predicate on Boolean assignments to natural-number variables, let $q$ and $r$ be finite quantifier prefixes, and let $	ext{ let }
\sigma$ be an assignment with starting index $i$. Truth of the concatenated prefix $q$ followed by $r$ under $	ext{ let }
\sigma$ at index $i$ is equivalent to truth of $q$ under $	ext{ let }
\sigma$ at index $i$, with the predicate that the remaining prefix $r$ is true starting at index $i+|q|$.
